{"id":"13A","title":"The Biblical Work Ethic","part":{"n":13,"title":"Labor & work"},"url":"/law/13-labor-work/13a","entries":[{"id":"13A.1","text":"Whatever work you put your hands to, do it with all your might.","refs":[{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":9,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"Eccl. 9:10."},{"id":"13A.2","text":"Every man should enjoy the good of all his labor.","refs":[{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":2,"verses":"24"},{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":3,"verses":"13"},{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":5,"verses":"18"}],"citation":"Eccl. 2:24; Eccl. 3:13; Eccl. 5:18."},{"id":"13A.3","text":"The laborer is worthy of his hire (wages).","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":10,"verses":"10"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":20,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":10,"verses":"7"},{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":5,"verses":"18"}],"citation":"Matt. 10:10; Matt. 20:8; Luke 10:7; 1 Tim. 5:18."},{"id":"13A.4","text":"We are exhorted to walk in a manner worthy of the vocation with which we have been called.","refs":[{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":4,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"Eph. 4:1."},{"id":"13A.5","text":"Every man shall receive his own reward according to his own labor.","refs":[{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":3,"verses":"8"}],"citation":"1 Cor. 3:8."},{"id":"13A.6","text":"If any would not work, neither should he eat.","refs":[{"book":"2 Thessalonians","chapter":3,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"2 Thes. 3:10."},{"id":"13A.7","text":"Lead a quite life, mind your own business, and work with your own hands.","refs":[{"book":"1 Thessalonians","chapter":4,"verses":"11"}],"citation":"1 Thes. 4:11."},{"id":"13A.8","text":"Be not slothful in business, but be fervent in spirit.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":12,"verses":"11"}],"citation":"Rom. 12:11."},{"id":"13A.9","text":"Do not engage in work and labor that is vain or futile.","refs":[{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":10,"verses":"3"}],"citation":"Jer. 10: 3."}]}